[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Nothing outside a plan may depend on a plan node

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS
TITLE: Nothing outside a plan may depend on a plan node
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: human
STATEMENT: >>>
Settled architecture, source annotations, and other plans must not hold
relations into a plan's nodes. A plan may depend outward; nothing may depend
inward.

Externality is a property of the FILE a node lives in, not of the node's type
or of its machinery. Plans and specifications use the same nodes, the same
edges and the same fingerprints; what differs is retention. Three retention
classes exist today: a plan directory under docs/plans/<plan>/, collectable as
a unit, which is also the containment unit DEC-PLAN-SCOPED-BACKLOG already
scopes its queries to; docs/spec/, durable specification; and **/.sdoc/,
settled architecture that outlives the plan that produced it and moves with its
package. A reference is external when its target lives in a plan directory and
its source does not live in that SAME plan directory.

Plan-to-plan is therefore exactly the violation spec-to-plan is, not a lesser
one. A peer plan is no more durable than the plan it cites, so a citation
between two plans strands on whichever of them is collected first.

Two kinds of reference are in scope, and both are keyed on a UID:

- a Parent relation, whatever its ROLE;
- a PARENT_FP entry, which is a dependency on that parent's contract.

File relations are out of scope. A File VALUE is a path, never a UID, so a File
relation cannot reference a plan node at all. Whether a File VALUE may name a
path under docs/plans/ is a separate rule about what a node may claim as its
implementation, and is not this invariant.

Source annotations -- a UID named in a comment in a source file -- are in scope
by intent and unenforceable today, because nothing turns them into edges. They
enter scope unchanged, with no rewording of this rule, on the day a
source-comment extractor exists. That is DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION's own retirement
condition.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Follows directly from plans being collectable. If a plan can be deleted or
never committed, an inbound reference is a dangling relation waiting to happen
-- and because a dangling relation is a hard export error, one collected plan
would break the build for everything that cited it.

Fingerprints are in scope for the opposite reason. A dangling relation fails
loudly; a dangling fingerprint does not fail at all, because PARENT_FP is a
String field the parser never resolves. So relations make a collected plan a
build break and fingerprints make it a silent rot, and only the second one
survives a green run.

Keying the rule on the containing file rather than on the node's type is what
lets it survive DEC-PLAN-LIFECYCLE-OPEN's narrowing. That decision established
that plans are not structurally different from specifications -- same nodes,
same edges, same machinery -- and left only retention open. A rule phrased in
terms of what a plan node IS would have had nothing left to say after that
narrowing. A rule phrased in terms of where a node lives keeps working, and
keeps working if a retention class is renamed or a fourth one appears.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Measured 2026-08-27 over a full clean export, before the one-node-per-file
carve: 139 nodes in 9 documents. The coordinates below were re-anchored onto the
carved files, and the edges themselves are unchanged -- the carve moved no
relation. The
UID-to-file map was built by grepping ^UID: across the tree, because the JSON
export carries no document path -- a document is TITLE, GRAMMAR and NODES only
-- the same gap MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK records.

Nodes per retention class: docs/plans/strictdoc-tooling 113,
docs/plans/beads-migration 18, docs/spec 4, packages/semble/.sdoc 4.

95 relations: 3 File, 92 Parent. Seven Parent relations cross a class. Five are
outward and legal: SLICE-SDOC-IN-SEMBLE Crosses both semble mechanisms;
SPIKE-EXECUTABLE-RULES and MECH-SEMANTICS-DEFINITION-BOUNDARY are Governed_By
DEC-SYSTEM-PURPOSE; MECH-SDOC-SKILL-CORRECTIONS Guarantees
INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE. Two violate, both plan-to-plan and both from
beads-migration into strictdoc-tooling: MECH-RENDER-CACHE Assumes MECH-FP-CHECK
(mech-render-cache.sdoc:33) and MECH-CORPUS-EDGE-MAP Assumes MECH-CYCLE-CHECK
(mech-corpus-edge-map.sdoc:44). Inbound edges from docs/spec/ or **/.sdoc/ into
any plan: zero.

31 PARENT_FP entries. One crosses a class -- SPIKE-EXECUTABLE-RULES to
DEC-SYSTEM-PURPOSE -- and it is outward. Inbound: zero. MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK's
STATEMENT scopes itself to relations only; fingerprints are the half that fails
silently and the check must cover both.

All three File relations point into packages/semble/. None names a path under
docs/plans/.

59 source-comment citations of strictdoc-tooling plan UIDs appear in 30 files
outside the graph -- checks/, dev/scripts/, dev/tasks/, devenv.nix, flake.nix,
overlays/dev-tools/strictdoc.nix, packages/strictdoc-grammar/. Several name the
plan file path beside the UID, for example overlays/dev-tools/strictdoc.nix
citing SLICE-STRICTDOC-OVERLAY with its document path -- which the carve then
had to rewrite, in all 17 places a citation named one of the ten deleted
documents. None is an edge today.
All 59 become inbound violations the day an extractor reads them.

Four export measurements on a scratch copy, clean output directory each time,
baseline exit 0:

- A Parent VALUE naming a nonexistent UID exits 1: "Requirement
  MECH-SEMBLE-EXTRA-GRAMMARS references parent requirement which doesn't exist".
  This is the loud half, and it is the fact the RATIONALE rests on.
- A File VALUE naming docs/plans/strictdoc-tooling/NO-SUCH-FILE.sdoc exits 0.
  File targets are not resolved at all; see MECH-FILE-RELATION-EXISTENCE.
- A PARENT_FP naming a nonexistent UID exits 0.
- An arch node given an Assumes relation into a plan node exits 0. The parser
  has no opinion on direction, so this invariant is enforceable only by our own
  check, which is INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE applied to this rule.

Positive control for those zero counts: the same scanner that reported no
inbound edges on the real graph flagged the injected arch-to-plan edge on the
fourth run, and reported the two plan-to-plan violations on both runs.

The previous NOTES said this needs design because it is unenforced and the
graph may already violate it. Both facts are true and neither is a design gap:
enforcement is MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK, and the two violations are recorded there.
What actually needed settling was the scope -- which reference kinds count, and
what makes one external once plans and specifications are the same machinery.

LEFT TO THE OPERATOR, deliberately. This milestone settles the plumbing;
each of these is a rule about how this instance works and milestone five is
where they get written.

- Whether docs/spec/ and **/.sdoc/ are one durable class or two ranked ones. This invariant only forbids depending INTO a plan; it deliberately does not say whether settled architecture may depend on durable specification, or the reverse. Today one edge exists in that space (MECH-SDOC-SKILL-CORRECTIONS Guarantees INV-GUARDS-MUST-EXECUTE, plan to spec) and none between arch and spec, so nothing forces the ranking yet. A full retention partial order is a semantics rule, not plumbing.

- Whether the 59 existing source annotations must be rewritten to name durable nodes before an extractor lands, or logged and left. This node states the rule and the trigger; it does not schedule the remediation.

- Whether a violation is a hard failure or a warning, and whether the two known plan-to-plan edges are grandfathered while the check goes in. That is MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK's severity policy and is left blank here deliberately.

- AUTHORED_BY on this node is currently human, and the proposed STATEMENT is llm-written prose that keeps the operator's original two sentences as its opening but adds four paragraphs beneath them. The key is the operator's to turn; flagging it rather than touching it.

AUTHORED_BY STILL READS human AND THE STATEMENT ABOVE IS NOT THE OPERATOR'S
PROSE. It was rewritten wholesale by a model during the 2026-08-27 grooming
pass, which preserved the node's intent and settled its interface but kept
almost none of its wording. The field was left alone because only the operator
turns it. Recorded here because MECH-AUTHORED-BY-GUARD is being built to catch
exactly this, and this pass produced eight instances of it while the question of
what the mark means was still open.

Retyped from INVARIANT to REQUIREMENT on 2026-08-30 (DEC-INVARIANT-IS-A-REQUIREMENT; DEC-NODE-FAMILIES). The UID keeps its retired prefix: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE.
<<<
